        ns2:claim "The paper argues against a simplistic structural copy of the environment and emphasizes behavioural equivalence (minimizing prediction error) rather than strict structural similarity. This challenges the notion that Active Inference necessarily leads to optimal decision-making as defined by achieving perfect veridical representation."^^xsd:string ;
