        ns2:claim "The paper discusses Active Inference as a general theory of behavior but doesn't explicitly address the universality claim of the FEP. It focuses on a specific application within a grid-world scenario."^^xsd:string ;
        ns2:confidence 6e-01 ;
        ns2:evidenceQuote "Active inference, regarded as a general theory of behaviour, offers a principled approach to probing the basis of sophistication in planning and decision-making."^^xsd:string ;
