        ns2:claim "The paper discusses a general updating process applicable across different probabilistic models, aligning with the broad scope of the FEP. However, it doesn't explicitly argue for universal applicability."^^xsd:string ;
        ns2:confidence 6e-01 ;
        ns2:evidenceQuote "It will be illustrated via a physical model involving (adapted) water flows through pipes with different diameters. Bayesian updating makes us wiser, in the sense that the posterior distribution makes the evidence more likely than the prior, since it incorporates the evidence."^^xsd:string ;
